{"version":"0.12.26","prev_tag":"v0.12.25","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"a6b1bc3dff4f826291ec094d7720adbf125777a8","title":"Discover and inspect lf commands, skills, and flows without launching them (#1353)","files":[".github/workflows/package-build.yml",".lf/flows/release-run.yaml",".lf/flows/telemetry-daily.yaml","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture.html","docs/architecture.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/lf-reference.md","docs/lf.md","python/tests/test_architecture.py","python/tests/test_release_automation.py","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/recovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-review.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/release-run.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/deploy.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/feature.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/refresh.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/ship-demo.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/ship.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/error.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow/saved_skill.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_graph.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/invocation.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/target.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/transitions.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/list.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/navigation.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/cron.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow_run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/durable.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/cli_discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/discovery_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/doctor_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","scripts/check_architecture.py","wave/growth/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"6d4727d33f1101d5cc7e01143878f95c8db1ccd2","title":"Keep managed Codex accounts tied to the intended login (#1355)","files":["TESTING.md","docs/subscriptions.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth_status.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account/identity.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_auth/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/provider_account_identity__d4aaef052408ce8d01965aa702a3b4e6.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/subscription.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/agent_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/auth_tests.rs","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1353,"title":"Discover and inspect lf commands, skills, and flows without launching them","body":"Finding the right `lf` invocation required knowing command ownership and how skills and flows competed for names. This PR adds local discovery and inspection, accepts unambiguous command shortcuts, and makes definition selection consistent across CLI execution and flow composition.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add `lf list`, `lf help NAME`, and `lf help --all`, showing definition sources and usable invocations without launching agents, connecting accounts, or fetching definitions.\n- Resolve unique shortcuts such as `lf land` to `lf pr land`; ambiguous names report canonical choices. Commands retain precedence over definitions.\n- Add `lf run NAME` and make untyped definition lookup prefer flows. Explicit `lf skill NAME` and `lf flow NAME` select only that kind; malformed flows report errors instead of falling back to skills.\n- Share one executable target model across CLI selection and flow composition while retaining captured instructions and existing saved-plan encoding for resume.\n- Replace authored YAML `op:` steps with `cmd:` and migrate bundled flows. External skills now use the same frontmatter parsing on fetch and cache reads.\n- Add the `pr-review` skill for HTML code walkthroughs and split CLI documentation into a workflow guide and command reference.\n\nExisting scripts using `lf catalog` must switch to `lf list`; custom flows must replace `op:` with `cmd:`. Same-named flows now take precedence over skills. The documentation also contains labeled design previews: proposed command-owner moves and overview commands remain unimplemented.\n\n## Checks\n\nInspected regression coverage for local inspection, ambiguity, definition precedence, external-skill parsing, and saved execution compatibility. Tests were not run for this description.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed here: run `lf list`, then `lf help feature` to inspect the workflow and its invocation without starting it. Run `lf land --help` to see help for the canonical `lf pr land` command.\n\nTracked by LOO-337: https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-337\n","files":[],"additions":3802,"deletions":3323,"changed_files":61,"merge_commit":"a6b1bc3dff4f826291ec094d7720adbf125777a8"},{"number":1355,"title":"Keep managed Codex accounts tied to the intended login","body":"Managed Codex accounts could display a configured email as verified while using a different login. This PR checks the credential’s identity before connecting, accepting verified usage, or routing Codex work, and reports mismatches with recovery commands.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Verify managed account identity on connect, status and routing · LOO-339](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-339/verify-managed-account-identity-on-connect-status-and-routing)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Validate Codex’s reported email against its native credential and per-user identity. Claude connect/import and explicit verification use the provider’s profile email and UUID.\n- Reject duplicate managed logins and misleading email changes. Different people sharing a workspace remain valid; staged reconnect preserves the installed credential while authorization waits.\n- Persist observed identity and plan without resetting account configuration or cooldowns. Temporary verification outages preserve cached credential health; provider rejection marks credentials missing.\n- Prefer observed Pro plans before Plus among healthy automatic Codex candidates, preserving explicit preferences and Session pins.\n- Keep ordinary status read-only, show usage as used/left, and display expired usage windows as unknown. JSON retains dated observations, so consumers must check reset timestamps.\n\nAccount state remains local to each Home. [Account usability follow-ups · LOO-340](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-340) owns shared state, current status by default, sole browser ownership, and Claude cached identity/routing. Native provider credential writers do not participate in Loopflow’s installation lock.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded branch validation, not rerun for this description:\n\n- Isolated Rust suite: 2,192 passed, 13 skipped, including all seven public auth tests.\n- Website: 78 passed, 3 skipped. Formatting, all-target Clippy, architecture, migration history, and fresh-Home JSON checks passed.\n- The original gate receipt remains failed. An earlier run launched real Claude because inherited executable selection overrode fixtures; the group was stopped and isolated checks subsequently passed. `TESTING.md` records the required isolation. See the preserved [review and gate evidence](https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/blob/8973f689a9e11a83b2dfa467fecddd095940d435/scratch/verify-managed-account-identity-on-review.md).\n\nIdentity proofs use synthetic fixtures; live OAuth and deployed acceptance remain unverified. Swift, app/UI, Python, and slow E2E remain with CI.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed live: run `lf auth status codex` to see the credential’s observed login and recovery guidance for any mismatch without starting Codex. Then run `lf auth status codex --verify` to request current identity and usage; a disagreeing login should be rejected rather than displayed as active (verified).","files":[],"additions":1490,"deletions":274,"changed_files":15,"merge_commit":"6d4727d33f1101d5cc7e01143878f95c8db1ccd2"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.25\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.25 keeps Task review close to the work and removes repeated preparation from delivery. The Mac app adds file editing beside Task conversations, while consolidated workflows reconcile plans, code, and memory before validation. Landing preserves unchanged commits, published descriptions, and merge-queue progress; verification reuses matching builds and evidence with clearer delivery measurements.\n\n## Review and edit without leaving the Task\n\nThe Mac app now places scratch notes, changed files, and an editable file view beside the Task’s retained terminals. Files and terminals follow the selected Task’s checkout.\n\n- **Show Files** provides recursive scratch navigation, changed files, and a PR link. Compare against the recorded PR base (**Parent**) or **HEAD**; **Diff** includes unsaved edits without writing them to disk.\n- Drafts, selection, and Undo survive switching files or Tasks within a window. Autosave runs after two quiet seconds; disable **Autosave Task Files** to save explicitly with ⌘S.\n- External changes arrive live. Disjoint local edits survive; disk changes win overlaps. Revision-checked saves retain submitted drafts, displaced files, and recovery receipts.\n- `lf task changes`, `diff`, and `file` gain comparison and file support; `lf task save` adds saving through recorded local placement without planning sync or starting a Run.\n\n## Reconcile work before delivery\n\n`realign` becomes the builtin owner for updating plans, code, and Wave memory. Consolidated repair and operating skills reduce overlapping entry points and make delivery stopping points explicit.\n\n- `realign` replaces `review-slice`, `refresh-plan`, `update-wave`, and `record-learnings`, preserving accepted requirements, unresolved evidence, and remaining work in existing artifacts.\n- `refresh` runs rebase → realign. Queue preparation runs compress → refresh → gate, so reconciliation happens before validation. Pursue passes refresh before convergence and publication; build and slice also make publication explicit.\n- `lf pr open` creates a draft and preserves existing readiness. `lf pr publish` promotes drafts; a failed promotion retains draft copy for retry.\n- Use `unbreak` to restore broken workflows and `debug` to investigate and fix code failures. `incident` composes unbreak → 5whys → launch-plan.\n- `lf vsm-operate` adds a manual repository pass through delivery, coordination, capacity, adaptation, and identity using independently callable S1–S5 skills. `wave/operate` applies the same questions within one Wave while preserving independent Task progress.\n\n## Keep useful CI work through landing\n\nFinal preparation and landing now preserve work that still applies to the current head. Merge-queue waiting, GitHub observations, and CI reuse are coordinated without treating stale or missing evidence as a pass.\n\n- Resuming a clean, armed or queued standalone PR retains its head and CI. Final preparation also preserves a single authored commit when its source and base are unchanged; necessary rebases and multi-commit normalization remain.\n- When local and remote heads match, final preparation retains GitHub’s title and body. Explicit copy and valid gate output take precedence; changed local heads generate fresh copy.\n- PRs waiting to enter the merge queue can remain behind main without an unnecessary rebase. Real conflicts and failed checks still receive recovery before entry; queued work waits for GitHub’s integrated result.\n- Landing and release read merge state and queue membership together, avoiding a false missing-request failure when a PR merges between reads. Required gates and repair details come from one check set for the observed head, with pagination and moving-head handling.\n- Main can reuse a successful merge-group CI run for the exact pushed SHA. Missing, failed, mismatched, or unreadable proof runs the full matrix. PRs and merge groups retain full checks; main still fills missing shared build caches.\n- Rust, SwiftPM, and Xcode caches account for their relevant profiles, source inputs, and toolchains. CI reuses already-built CLI and app binaries; native captures run two at a time while retaining all eight images and comparisons.\n\n## Measure delivery from current Run evidence\n\nScheduled telemetry now reads the current Run ledger instead of the removed `agent_turns` table. Reports distinguish measured intervals from missing evidence and avoid assigning performance passes to unbudgeted samples.\n\n- The scorecard reports ended-Run duration, direct usage, and recorded Task PR creation, publication, and landing intervals.\n- **Recorded agent attempt → merge** joins provider attempts to exact managed Task PRs and reports measured/eligible coverage, including earlier and unfinished Runs. It is an observed lower bound: missing history or standalone work can hide an earlier start. Unstarted prepared Sessions remain unknown; Task PR creation → merge remains the durable baseline.\n- Date- and ownership-scoped Run queries filter manifests before parsing unrelated event histories, retaining usage, ordering, and evidence-gap behavior.\n- Expensive CI commands log CPU time, memory accounting, faults, and context switches alongside elapsed time. These peaks do not measure simultaneous host memory.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **Custom workflows and installed skills:** retired names have no compatibility aliases. Update custom Flow references and sync installed skill exports separately. Captured Flows retain pinned instructions. Manual S1–S5 operation adds no scheduling or channel delivery; its full evidence handoff and the incident handoff remain unproven end to end in the supplied record.\n- **Task file limits:** editing supports complete UTF-8 files up to 1 MB. Unsaved drafts do not survive window closure. Recovery storage has no automatic cleanup and disappears with the worktree; it does not guarantee exclusion of concurrent writers or power-loss durability. Extremely long lines can remain slow.\n- **Saved Sessions:** returned `open_argv` carries the original executable, Home, and database across installation changes. Retained launches require valid receipts and unchanged artifacts; listing still uses the selected installation. `lf session open <id> --json` prepares the handoff; execute its returned argv to open the conversation. Returned launch failures remain journaled after retry. The complete installation-switch journey and real Ghostty open/resume remain unverified.\n- **Disk headroom:** fresh verification reclaims eligible inactive build caches unchanged for 24 hours toward 64 GiB free and stops below 32 GiB. Active and recent builds remain protected. Busy uv caches fail pruning immediately so other cleanup can proceed; recent gate output no longer consumes cleanup capacity without an eligible removal.\n- **Performance evidence:** build caches need an initial cold fill, and hosted warm reuse remains unverified for the Swift/Xcode changes. Local native capture comparisons fell from about 28 seconds to 14 seconds with identical images. These measurements and the recorded reader/build improvements do not establish an overall time-to-merge reduction. Added Swift failure logs improve diagnosis; the reported hosted hang is not claimed fixed.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- Store validation embeds the canonical schema reference at build time, reuses constructed references for other migration paths, and reduces checksum bookkeeping while still checking each actual database. Shipped migration SQL and receipt bytes are unchanged.\n- Development and test builds optimize bundled SQLite. Cargo avoids rebuilds caused by absent packed refs or unrelated loose-branch commits while retaining provenance updates for the current checkout and tags.\n- Native Task proof waits stop when their condition succeeds. Wave selection tests no longer depend on creation order, candidate-release tests avoid unrelated merge polling, and doctor tests fetch isolated local remotes instead of mutating a shared checkout.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":0,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}